\pard\plain \li950\ri1757\sa160\sl259\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Captain, the cavity is just up ahead, 20 meters out\u8221\'94. John slowed his pace to a quiet walk upon Tao\u8217\'92s announcement, the others meeting his pace. They were silent, rolling their feet onto the ground as they walked so no sudden cracks from the rock bed beneath them might announce their presence. Their suit\u8217\'92s heel\u8217\'92s articulated with every tendon\u8217\'92s pull and ease. \u8220\'932 meters\u8221\'94 Tao whispered. John looked ahead but saw nothing. He wasn\u8217\'92t surprised though given what had just transpired. He knew the technology's capabilities. \u8220\'93It should be right here\u8221\'94 Tao\u8217\'92s words gently flowed from her mouth as heat expelled from her helmet\u8217\'92s exhaust vents. A cold wind rose from silence stirring around them, a small howl erupted, ripping through the valley stirring up snow from the ground, shedding any stray icicles to thin from the cliff's face.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Our suit\u8217\'92s power reserves cores have been exhausted, We won\u8217\'92t last much longer out here in the cold\u8221\'94. In response John raised his hand to hip height, his fingers splayed out level with the ground. He was silent, still, the others waited with anticipation. He took two more steps closer still with his left shoulder to the cliff face. He raised his rifle barrel then poked the cliff face with his rifle muzzle, although as he suspected his muzzle didn\u8217\'92t meet the sound of crunching steel against rock, but the soft static crackle that he had heard when the debris fell through their own Mesh. His muzzle dipped into the cliff like a stick in a still pool of water. \u8220\'93This is it\u8221\'94 John stepped back, ice crushing beneath his heel as his weight sunk into the piling snow. \u8220\'93Your up techy!\u8221\'94, }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tau knelt down into the snow crushing it beneath her,gleaning into her wrist terminal. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Prepping echo\u8221\'94 She took a moment to think then began tapping away again \u8220\'93Annnnd.. that should do it!\u8221\'94 her voice seemed a little less confident this time but confident enough. \u8220\'93Confirm flight plan\u8221\'94 pulsed on her wrist terminal. \u8220\'93What\u8217\'92s the hold up\u8221\'94 said John \u8220\'93I needed to set a recorded flight path for the time I\u8217\'92ll pilot it manually through the Mesh. Once on the other side I\u8217\'92ll lose comms due to the sound barrier, it will finish it\u8217\'92s scan then return to the recorded flight paths final origin then exit, I just threw the vectors in reverse so it comes out when comes back to the other side of the Mesh. \u8220\'93Oo k\u8221\'94 Said John, pretending to understand. \u8220\'93it should stop recording a second after it enters the mesh or loses comms either way we will get her back\u8221\'94 Tao seemed more confident now she had reassured herself it seemed. Shai looked back at Tex, Tex shrugged his shoulders.   }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Deploying Echo\u8221\'94 Tao moved smoothly in her actions. From the rear of her suit\u8217\'92s shoulder blade, the same port the peregrine had ejected from slid open, each blade which formed the port window retracting within the suit\u8217\'92s armoured shell. Everything about the port seal had been carefully crafted. The edges of the seal blades pushed outward against the edge of the next blade, meaning that any positive pressure from within the suit would force a seal in a vacuum environment, making it user friendly in space. Shai found her confidence in the Mark IV increasing as she observed the intricate operation. Before John had even given a thought to what could possibly lie behind the mesh, a light whisper hummed over his shoulder. A small drone no larger than the size of a rhinoceros beetle buzzed past vanishing into the mesh consumed by the cliff face as the ripples from it\u8217\'92s wake dissipated in microseconds into an illusion. To the human eye the small glitch in the mesh couldn\u8217\'92t be seen. Only visible really by the high frequency echo location scanners performed by sonic sensors. A trained engineer might pick up on the pattern, although to anyone else.. it appeared merely as instrument sound without proper curve fitting transforms. Tao had proven this earlier. The inbuilt autopilot program of the Echo had not been designed to detect these \u8220\'93light mesh\u8221\'94 instances yet alone pass through them. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ve lost contact with the drone\u8221\'94, said Tao tapping away on her terminal, her suit activating sentry mode as she became occupied with the task ahead. \u8220\'93What\u8217\'92s the hold up\u8221\'94 John was getting impatient, \u8220\'93We wait for the data link when it gets back\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93How\u8221\'94, Tao intervened \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92d say a minute at most\u8221\'94. Tex and Shai were huddled together up against the cliff face. \u8220\'93Starting to Prune up in this Dam suit\u8221\'94 Tex groaned moving in discomfort. \u8220\'93Big guy wants some action\u8221\'94 Chuckled Shai softly under her voice. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Careful what you wish for\u8221\'94. Tao had a certain unease in her tone, her head fixed still in her wrist terminal. \u8220\'93My suits long range scanners have picked up the engine signature of the LRD from earlier\u8221\'94 This time she was less calm, but still controlled. \u8220\'93Persistent fucker!\u8221\'94 Said John, \u8220\'93I thought we shook that thing already\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s Engineer probably picked up on the impulse anomaly I detected earlier\u8221\'94 Tao flicked her HUD view to the others. \u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s turned around for a second run, heading our way\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We\u8217\'92re sitting ducks here\u8221\'94, Said John as he nodded over at Tex triggering him to reach for his Railstorm. \u8220\'93Power reserve for hard light mesh will only give us about 10 seconds of concealment Cap\u8221\'94 Kitten had understood the stress in John\u8217\'92s tone anticipating his question before he\u8217\'92d even asked.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 the charging of coils let out a winding high pitched humm. Tex mounted the Railstorm on his shoulder. His eyes fixated through the targeting reticle on the ridge lying in wait for the drone\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s return run. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'9320 seconds John till we\u8217\'92re in short range scanners\u8221\'94. Tau seemed calm more than the others. \u8220\'93I think I\u8217\'92d rather take my chances with what's on the other side\u8221\'94, said John, \u8220\'93Second that\u8221\'94 said Tex, still with his sites locked on the ridge above. A second later a crackling static let out startling John. He stood back locking his sites on the the ripples of where echo had just zipped out of. Echo had emerged from the mesh unscathed, it stopped, pivoted on it\u8217\'92s axis then headed straight towards Tau. Like a friendly companion it tapped it\u8217\'92s docking bay on the back of her suit then re-coupled with it\u8217\'92s landing arm. The arm drew the drone back into Tau\u8217\'92s suit ready to be deployed again. \u8220\'93Collating the data, I need a few seconds\u8221\'94. \u8220\'93Get it done\u8221\'94 John seemed collected, but you could hear the grinding in his tone alone. A frustration of silence lingered among the others as tension built in the air. \u8220\'93The structure inside seems natural but.. scans picked up heartbeat harmonics of a life-form..  it appears to be.. human\u8221\'94. John turned his head to Shai, confused more than concerned \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll take my chances with a human over an assault Drone\u8221\'94. John\u8217\'92s rifle muzzle dipped into the cliff wall like a like a drop entering a pool. ripples rose up humming from the entry point with a wave of crackling static. As he stepped through the mesh his body gradually disappeared swallowed by the cliff face leaving behind a silent wisp. The static crackling stopped.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tao, Shai and Tex all filed in behind where John had just entered, Tex walking backwards letting the suit\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s suggested kinematics pairing with Shai. The formed retreat closed out the sky ridges tightly as Tex\u8217\'92s shoulder turrets watched in opposing directions gyrating along the walls seamlessly. The hum down of Tex\u8217\'92s Railstorm cells brought the tunnel to a silence. Charged hydrogen focused light beams packed enough electrons in the punch to disable any incoming drone within milliseconds. Tao had worked on the development of the charging system herself, although she kept this to herself. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Shai was busy looking at her HUD\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s life form signatures within their proximity watching for any unwanted visitors. \u8220\'93John, that life form echo picked up I\u8217\'92m running it through the computer\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93That LRD will be at the mesh by now not far behind us\u8221\'94 said Tau abruptly. \u8220\'93We should keep moving\u8221\'94 said John. \u8220\'93We don\u8217\'92t know how, inquisitive our old friend will be\u8221\'94. He raised his sites moving forward in a smooth motion. After a few steps into the tunnels depths a beam of red light shot out scanning the wall directly in front of him, his armours outline shadowed on the wall within the scan print, Whatever it was, he was in it\u8217\'92s sites, he knew this It wasn\u8217\'92t his rifles targeting laser or any of the others scanning arrays it was too large. John stopped dead in his tracks taking to the ground immediately. \u8220\'93Take cover!\u8221\'94 The red cone of lasers flickered past him deeper into the tunnel. John turned around on the ground, aiming his sites at the direction of the tunnel entrance. An explosion erupted through the cave sending rocks and debris on his back and pummelling directly into the others who were now huddled against the tunnel walls where what small crevasses offered minimal protection. John didn\u8217\'92t hesitate, returning fire at the large metallic monstrosities sensor dish. Sparks flew from the drone around it\u8217\'92s shell as what remained of it\u8217\'92s rear slowly emerged through the hard light mesh. The heavily armoured assault sparrow forced it\u8217\'92s way deeper scraping the tunnel walls in it\u8217\'92s wake to the sound of grinding steel and rock. \u8220\'93It must have detected the curtain breaks in the mesh when we entered the cave\u8221\'94 shouted Tau.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 They had nowhere to go. If they stepped out that would be the end. John\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s shoulder turrets were both firing rapidly, sending a barrage of fire at the drone scattering any proper reading it could make out ahead. \u8220\'93I can only suppress it for so long, it\u8217\'92s armour is too thick\u8230\'85 Tex!\u8221\'94 Shouted John. Tex  reached back over his shoulder and retrieved his Storm Rail. He clenching his fist around the Storm rail\u8217\'92s handle waiting for a break in the curtain of fire. \u8220\'93Hold fire\u8221\'94 Kitten chimed in an almost complete calm monotone pleasantly easing the tension as John and his team regained their focus. The LRD was at a stand still, re-priming it\u8217\'92s cannon, echoes of charging wires hummed through the tunnel.  The sound of Tex\u8217\'92s Railstorm charging had complimented that of the Drones, He wouldn\u8217\'92t let it have a chance to open fire again. Collected he stepped out with the drone clear in his Storm Rail\u8217\'92s site. His would sing first and have the final clap as it\u8217\'92s coils let out a loud clap through the tunnel behind him. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The drone shuddered in it\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s place moving from side to side crashing into the walls, disoriented  like a drunken belter trying to find his way home from the star bar. It moaned in electronic groans and splutters, as it\u8217\'92s main turret powered down.}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cb4\highlight4  }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cb4\highlight4 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It still has it\u8217\'92s kinetic turret!\u8221\'94 Tau was trying to contain herself, sweat ran down her forehead as the held back the images from her blown apart comrades that took blows from rail rifles in the previous war. It wasn\u8217\'92t pretty watching your closest friend be ripped in two, their organs splayed out on the ground by a 12 inch thick iron slug leaving an unscheduled painting along the hull of an Icarus. She knew that while they might survive most shock penetrations now with the new suit\u8217\'92s built nervous network, in the moment they would not be able to recover to finish the job. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s video feeds are disabled but I\u8217\'92m still picking up a sounding scan\u8221\'94, Tau held her breath, speaking quietly. Their Mark IV suit\u8217\'92s dampened out any internal sounds, but instinct still took over as though they were hiding their frail exposed bodies, Shai turned her attention to her heartbeat scanner heightening the tension in her voice. \u8220\'93Aah guys, that life form I picked up earlier it\u8217\'92s getting closer, it\u8217\'92s coming from the other side of the tunnel, We\u8217\'92ll be pinched\u8221\'94. Tex began reaching for a slug to load into the Railstorm\u8217\'92s kinetic chamber. \u8220\'93Whatever it is, it\u8217\'92s not going to like what I\u8217\'92ve got in store\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93Stay where you are Tex! That drone can still turn you to pink mist!\u8221\'94 said Tau frantically, Tex chambered the slug in his Storm rail then hugged his back hard up against the tunnel wall. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93The signal.. it appears to be human\u8221\'94, Said Shai. She looked up at Tex from the other side of the tunnel, her voice edged mixed with relief to confusion. \u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s\u8230\'85 it\u8217\'92s getting closer, 20 meters and closing on our 6\u8221\'94. John remained fixed in position, prone his sites perched still fixed on the drones direction. His shoulder turret pivoted 180 degrees covering the rear of the tunnel behind them. \u8220\'93I got it covered, we have bigger problems right now, focus on that fucking drone\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 Said John.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Everything was quiet, awkwardly quiet. The Sparrow hovered vigilantly, fixed, waiting for a positive read to be picked up on one of John\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s team. \u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s operating on Autopilot\u8221\'94 Tau began to explain but more for herself than anything \u8220\'93It must have lost contact with command when it crossed the mesh barrier\u8221\'94 She whispered, then the tunnel fell to silence once more. The walls began to vibrate and hum, like the mountain was becoming alive, gently. A loud thud shook the tunnel sending rubble and debris clamouring over their armoured suit\u8217\'92s. An ensemble of metallic clangs as their suit\u8217\'92s took the grunt of the falling debris announced their positions even more. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s trying to echo-locate us!\u8221\'94 said John. \u8220\'93Fuck this!\u8221\'94 said Tex, reluctant to stand there like a rabbit in the headlight. They all knew the sparrow would soon determine their positions with it\u8217\'92s advanced AI, differentiating the sound of rubble against steel would be no hard feat. Tex had waited long enough in his mind, He selected the highest charge possible on the Rail Storm, and listened to the purr of the  coils as they began to prime, just enough, then kneeled down in the open of the tunnel, Storm Rail at the ready, converging his targeting reticle on the sparrows main processing unit. \u8220\'93Covering Fire!\u8221\'94 yelled John. Instantly Tau pivoted from the left side of the tunnel just off to the front left of Tex raising her rifle as she did in a smooth motion. The spacing was tight between them, with just enough opening for John to lay down fire between Tex and Tau, an unconventional and completely unorthodox manoeuvre by any training standard, but what choice did they have?}
\par\pard\plain \li950\ri1757\ql\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 A barrage of fire opened up toward the Sparrow as soon as John had gave the order. Sparks of splintering, hot molten amber ricochet off the armour cladded drone as John and Taus Sherpa rounds did nothing to damage the drone. It was akin to throwing sand in the face of the schoolyard bully, only delaying a heavy handed punch to the face. The sparrows sensor arrays lit up, overwhelmed by molten rain, it\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s scans became completely useless. Tex watched on anxiously, as the Storm Rail hummed while it charged for it\u8217\'92s next shot, seconds felt like days, as he willed the last bar of the charge gauge in his HUD to green light him so he could let all hell loose. Tex\u8217\'92s sights finally fixed their lock on the target with a lock. Meanwhile Shai observed the sparrows targeting lasers track up along his chest, but the reticle didn\u8217\'92t stop there; it kept rising up past Tex, past John, flickering through the billowing fog deeper into the tunnel where a deep recessed void appeared that hadn\u8217\'92t been there before. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Storm Rail Charged\u8221\'94 strobed in the top left of Tex\u8217\'92s HUD, Suddenly in a bright unison flash of blue and amber, the tunnel walls lit up in rapid succession. Blinding the others from both directions within milliseconds of the other. The Sparrow let loose it\u8217\'92s Kinetic rifle, Tex steadfast in his firing stance arched back slightly as a thick metal slug left the Storm-rails barrel. A tight crisp cloud of steam tailing it\u8217\'92s trail.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cb5\highlight5 Tex felt a  percussive ripple fl}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 y through his suit, sending tingles down his spine. A scattered shock wave belted through the tunnel with a deafening disorienting effect. Adrenaline coursed through his body, sending tingles down his veins from head to toe. Tex closed his eyes, and thought of what it would be like to die, imagining the emptiness of it. He knew if he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d failed in his shot, the others wouldn\u8217\'92t stand a chance. He thought he was done for anyway, so he took the risk to save them, and he found comfort knowing they might make it out alive. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\pard\plain \li950\ri1757\sa160\sl259\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The Sparrow let out a howling bionic scream, jumbled static mixed with corrosive high pitched piezoelectric buzzing, gnawed at their skulls, seamlessly bypassing their suit\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s built in decibel filters. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 It stumbled uncontrollably, it\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s steaming railgun aimlessly spinning about flagging the others in the process, snapped and twisted against the tunnel walls into spaghetti as it thrashed about helplessly. Eventually it plummeted into rock and snow sending debris flying deeper into the tunnel peppering it\u8217\'92s targets.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tau gritted her teeth as she tweaked settings desperately to block out the frequencies. Finally the buzzing stopped, their ears still ringing with tinnitus as they reoriented. A softening static slipped from the tunnel as the machines last hum whispered down into the cold embracing of silence. For a split moment it felt like as though a ghost had escaped from its now lifeless armour cladded shell. It now laid peacefully blocking the tunnel entrance behind it. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tex\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s Storm-rail still had steam billowing from it\u8217\'92s glowing muzzle as it slowly found it\u8217\'92s resting place down his chest. His body like a ragdoll fell forward powerless, caught in a kneeling cradle hunched over his forward knee as he tried to move, but he felt no response. He could think of doing it, but his body remained still. His heavy head followed his chest dropping forward resting to the side against the shaft of the cooling Storm-rail. He gazed down at the ground, his thoughts began to wander aimlessly. The monstrosity clad in his oversized suit's thick armour knelt dead still, like a statue in the middle of the tunnel. The atmosphere from the entrance of the tunnel propelled forward like a small wave from the sparrows' impact. the waves of mist clashed around Tex, settling like a resting pool of fog by a sleeping obelisk, it rippled along his calves, kissing his lifeless hands gently. \u8220\'93Tex!!\u8221\'94 A tear forced its way out of Shai\u8217\'92s eye straddling the bottom of her eye lid, filled with the internal blue glow from within her helmet, a small galaxy seemed to flicker within it as all the body functions of her teammates pulsed in a barrage of information. She wasn\u8217\'92t checking them, She wasn\u8217\'92t thinking, she was in a sea of rage and sorrow. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 With Shai preoccupied and John still covering the front, Tau looked back through the thick fog at the rear of the tunnel. A burning blue glow caressed her gaze drawing her in. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93John\u8221\'94 Tau whispered  slowly, easing her way deeper toward the void. \u8220\'93There is something..\u8221\'94 she switched her HUD to thermals \u8220\'93someone..  behind us\u8221\'94. \u8220\'93Get it together Shai\u8221\'94 said John with sharp authority. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93OK, ok, ok cap\u8221\'94, Shai collected herself and began checking Tex\u8217\'92s vitals through her HUD. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m still picking up neural activity but it\u8217\'92s limited to involuntary functions, he\u8217\'92s still breathing\u8221\'94. John closed his eyes with a sigh of relief. \u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s locked in syndrome, His neural link was disconnected impromptu\u8230\'85 from an EMP charge..\u8221\'94 Said Shai.  \u8220\'93We took out that things fucking EMP!\u8221\'94, John\u8217\'92s voice tremored, he had done this as routine, he clawed in his mind at the possibility of a storm rail critical misfunction. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m tapping into his suit and initiating an emergency reboot\u8221\'94. Shai, was beginning to gain composure again. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cb5\highlight5 Tex, groaned, moaning in discomfort}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 , his eyes rolling from the back of his skull back to their resting place, druel dripped from his bottom lip. His jawline twitched as he observed a notification pulsing in his HUD. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Reboot initiated\u8221\'94. He felt the life pouring into the back of his neck like freezing water, then his shoulders, arms, torso, legs and eventually his toes. His body ached and burned buzzing and twitching, like a bed of needles pierced his soul as he urged himself forward, One knee up, then the next  he raised himself in agony from the ground.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What the fuck..\u8221\'94 Tex\u8217\'92s groaned in annoyance, as he locked his jaw back and forth regaining voluntary muscle control.. \u8220\'93That Sparrow take down \u8230\'85 Nice work! I didn\u8217\'92t even hit the darn thing, I lost control of my arms just as I pulled the trigger,\u8221\'94 his eyes drifted from what remained of a steaming splintered hulking wreck of the sparrow. His eyes climbed their way up the tunnels edge, eventually to find a watermelon sized cavity his stray shot had carved, the slug or what remained of it sitting proud in the middle of it. The cavity sat proud just above where the sparrow once hovered before it had dramatically met it\u8217\'92s end. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Johnnn!!\u8221\'94 Tau croaked with annoyance still trying to edge his attention. She had made her way to the rear of Tunnel, \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re going to want to see this.\u8221\'94 the sound of crushing ice and stone beneath her boots turned to a metallic thud. She knelt down, running her fingers through the ice and ruble to reveal an unnatural metallic floor.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Tex, realizing as his senses came too he was the only heavy gunner in the squad, turned about face throwing his storm-rail back on his shoulder it\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s reticle now locked directly on the void. Silence took a hold of them as they locked sites at the end of the tunnel in anticipation. Slowly, a falling belly of fog and steam spilled endlessly through a wall that seemed to breathe. }{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cb5\highlight5 By now the blue glow that had drawn Tau in had diminished to nothing. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Suddenly a belly of fog and steam hurled toward them from as the breathing wall gave way, scattering their sensors and vision. A cloak field like that at the face of the cliff powered down revealing an unnatural structure behind it, seemingly organic yet also steel. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cb5\highlight5  They could hardly believe what they were seeing. An EMP cannon the size of a minibus had been hidden within the tunnel. It\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s positioning  well planned. A defensive vantage point overlooking the tunnels opening, encapsulated behind a seamless cloaked wall with only an opening small enough to allow for the Cannons muzzle to sit ever so proudly, concealed behind the cloaking field which was no more. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The electric hum that had taken them by surprise eased down to a whispering static. Something was moving behind the turret, seated at it\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s control centre. Immediately rifle sites raised at the mysterious figure to the rear of the cannon as they hugged the walls of the void closing distance between them. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Waaaa hooooo!!, I\u8217\'92ve been waiting to use this bad boy for over a century now!\u8221\'94, A joyous victory chant filled the tunnel with a voice slightly inorganic. At John\u8217\'92s direction the others lowered their arms, Tex\u8217\'92s rifle still slightly raised untrusting. \u8220\'93A century yet before this cowboy leaves town you protectant genocidal bastards you!\u8221\'94 Tau look}}